#X obj 638 11 array.convolve;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 166 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object performs an FFT convolution of the target
array with an impulse response array. The target array is set with
the first argument (or the @array property) \, and the impulse response
is taken from the array given by the second argument (or the @ir property).
The convolution is started by a bang on the left inlet. When the process
finishes \, a bang is sent out through the outlet. If the @norm flag
is enabled \, the impulse response is normalized before convolution.;
